  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many hours Rebecca worked, we need to set up and solve a system of equations based on the information given.\n\nLet's define the variables:\n- \\( T \\) is the number of hours Thomas worked.\n- \\( B \\) is the number of hours Rebecca worked.\n- \\( R \\) is the number of hours Toby worked.\n\nFrom the problem, we know the following:\n1. The total number of hours worked by Thomas, Toby, and Rebecca is 157.\n2. Thomas worked \\( x \\) hours.\n3. Toby worked 10 hours less than twice what Thomas worked.\n4. Rebecca worked 8 hours less than Toby.\n\nWe can express these relationships with the following equations:\n1. \\( T + B + R = 157 \\)\n2. \\( R = 2T - 10 \\)\n3. \\( B = R - 8 \\)\n\nFirst, substitute the expression for \\( R \\) from equation 2 into equation 3:\n\\[ B = (2T - 10) - 8 \\]\n\\[ B = 2T - 18 \\]\n\nNow substitute the expressions for \\( T \\) and \\( B \\) into equation 1:\n\\[ x + (2T - 18) + (2T - 10) = 157 \\]\nCombine like terms:\n\\[ x + 4T - 28 = 157 \\]\nAdd 28 to both sides:\n\\[ x + 4T = 185 \\]\nSolve for \\( T \\):\n\\[ 4T = 185 - x \\]\n\\[ T = \\frac{185 - x}{4} \\]\n\nNow substitute \\( T = \\frac{185 - x}{4} \\) back into the expression for \\( B \\):\n\\[ B = 2T - 18 \\]\n\\[ B = 2 \\left( \\frac{185 - x}{4} \\right) - 18 \\]\n\\[ B = \\frac{2(185 - x)}{4} - 18 \\]\n\\[ B = \\frac{370 - 2x}{4} - 18 \\]\nConvert 18 to a fraction with a denominator of 4:\n\\[ B = \\frac{370 - 2x}{4} - \\frac{72}{4} \\]\nCombine the fractions:\n\\[ B = \\frac{370 - 2x - 72}{4} \\]\n\\[ B = \\frac{298 - 2x}{4} \\]\n\\[ B = \\frac{149 - x}{2} \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of hours Rebecca worked is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{149 - x}{2}}\\).",
